{"fetch_error_details function lacks explicit timeout handling and could amplify latency issues if nodestore is slow - needs timeout parameter with reasonable default (e.g., 500ms)": 0.17243190109729767, "fetch_error_details should implement graceful degradation to continue with breadcrumbs-only if the fetch fails or times out": 0.37876129150390625, "fetch_error_details missing metrics to track fetch latency and failure rates to detect nodestore performance issues": 0.13192027807235718, "Chronological merge assumes consistent timestamp semantics between error events and replay breadcrumbs - if systems use different time sources or precision, ordering may be incorrect": 0.05249415338039398, "Chronological merge needs deterministic tie-breaking logic (e.g., by event type or ID) when timestamps are equal": 0.018335208296775818, "Chronological merge should validate that timestamps are in a comparable format/timezone": 0.030785107985138893, "fromJSON() method now returns Visualize[] instead of single Visualize instance - breaking API change that will break code expecting single object": 0.7372792363166809, "Asymmetric compatibility where toJSON maintains legacy shape but fromJSON changes contract creates migration risk for persisted visualizations, URL parameters, and downstream consumers": 0.24330298602581024, "Changing from yAxes: readonly string[] to yAxis: string is breaking internal API change affecting ~20 files with risk for less-tested code paths and persisted query state": 0.19619964063167572, "Missing contract tests for round-trip serialization with both old and new payload formats to ensure compatibility": 0.04481153562664986, "Owner field update logic should enforce mutual exclusivity between owner_user_id and owner_team_id at model level, not just serializer - possible to end up with both fields set during concurrent updates": 0.24907523393630981, "Mutual exclusivity validation between age and timestamp checks self.initial_data in field validator, causing order-dependent validation behavior - should use validate() method for object-level validation": 0.5028853416442871, "isVisualize type guard changed to check for single yAxis string instead of yAxes array - objects with old shape will fail guard and be incorrectly classified if persisted state contains old format": 0.11349641531705856, "Logic change from map to flatMap combined with Visualize.fromJSON() returning array could lead to unexpected URL parameter multiplication and URL bloat": 0.1933019906282425}